--- make
description: A job in jobs/: a script that does one task and logs what it did, for a scheduler or by hand
category: Scripts and data
usage: <name> [--every "15 minutes"]
--every: How often it should run, noted in the file for cron or Task Scheduler
example: kscript make job send-reminders --every "1 day"
example: kscript make job cleanup/old-uploads
to: {{ paths.jobs }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}
hint: Run it: kscript {{ paths.jobs }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}{{#if every}} (schedule it every {{ every }} with cron or Task Scheduler){{/if}}
---
// {{ title }}: run it with kscript {{ paths.jobs }}/{{ dir }}{{ kebab }}{{ ext }}{{#if every}}, every {{ every }}{{/if}}.
// It logs to the terminal; set logging providers in config.yaml to keep a file (kscript make logger).
log "{{ title }} started"

// Do the work here.
done = 0

log(fields: { done: $done }) "{{ title }} finished"
